1
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:10,760
A market seller sells 9 boxes of mangoes.

2
00:00:10,810 --> 00:00:13,550
Each box costs 6 dollars 80.

3
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,240
Can you work out the total in your head?

4
00:00:16,290 --> 00:00:19,260
Pause the video and try.

5
00:00:19,310 --> 00:00:20,690
9 is nearly 10.

6
00:00:20,740 --> 00:00:26,110
And 10 boxes are easy: 10 times 6.80 is 68 dollars.

7
00:00:26,160 --> 00:00:28,200
That is one box too many.

8
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:29,870
So take one box off.

9
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:32,350
68 minus 6.80 is 61.20.

10
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:34,660
9 boxes cost 61 dollars 20.

11
00:00:34,710 --> 00:00:38,120
This trick is called compensation.

12
00:00:38,170 --> 00:00:39,950
Remember three useful laws.

13
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:41,980
You can multiply in any order.

14
00:00:42,030 --> 00:00:44,900
3 times 7 is the same as 7 times 3.

15
00:00:44,950 --> 00:00:46,860
You can group in any way.

16
00:00:46,910 --> 00:00:51,650
2 times 5, times 9, is the same as 2, times 5 times 9.

17
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:54,020
And you can split a number.

18
00:00:54,070 --> 00:00:58,170
6 times 14 is 6 times 10, plus 6 times 4.

19
00:00:58,220 --> 00:01:02,740
Compensation means: use a nearby round number, then adjust.

20
00:01:02,790 --> 00:01:07,710
9 times a number is 10 times the number, minus the number.

21
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:13,210
So 9 times 6.8 is 68 minus 6.8, which is 61.2.

22
00:01:13,260 --> 00:01:15,190
It works for 99 as well.

23
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:20,680
99 times a number is 100 times the number, minus the number.

24
00:01:20,730 --> 00:01:23,280
Here are three more strategies.

25
00:01:23,330 --> 00:01:25,880
First: a decimal is a division.

26
00:01:25,930 --> 00:01:28,530
0.06 is 6 divided by 100.

27
00:01:28,580 --> 00:01:34,690
So 0.06 times 3,500 is 6 times 35, which is 210.

28
00:01:34,740 --> 00:01:37,050
Second: split the divisor.

29
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:42,150
Dividing by 40 is the same as dividing by 4, then by 10.

30
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:47,790
13.6 divided by 4 is 3.4, and 3.4 divided by 10 is 0.34.

31
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:50,860
Third: re-order, to use an easy pair.

32
00:01:50,910 --> 00:01:53,570
0.25 times 4 is exactly 1.

33
00:01:53,620 --> 00:01:54,360
Your turn.

34
00:01:54,410 --> 00:01:57,840
Work out 0.5 times 4.6 times 2 in your head.

35
00:01:57,890 --> 00:02:01,380
Pause the video and try it.

36
00:02:01,430 --> 00:02:03,490
Do the easy pair first.

37
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:05,050
0.5 times 2 is 1.

38
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:07,800
Then 1 times 4.6 is 4.6.

39
00:02:07,850 --> 00:02:09,280
Here is the method.

40
00:02:09,330 --> 00:02:11,460
Step 1: look at the numbers.

41
00:02:11,510 --> 00:02:13,870
Is one close to a round number?

42
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:17,540
Is there a pair that makes 1, 10 or 100?

43
00:02:17,590 --> 00:02:19,370
Step 2: choose a strategy.

44
00:02:19,420 --> 00:02:24,450
Compensate, split, re-order, or write the decimal as a division.

45
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:28,790
Step 3: write down the steps, so you do not lose track.

46
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:31,760
Step 4: check with an estimate.

47
00:02:31,810 --> 00:02:35,530
Work out 0.25 times 9.7 times 4.

48
00:02:35,580 --> 00:02:36,610
Re-order it.

49
00:02:36,660 --> 00:02:38,580
Do 0.25 times 4 first.

50
00:02:38,630 --> 00:02:40,030
That is 1.

51
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:41,670
1 times 9.7 is 9.7.

52
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:45,420
Done, with no written multiplication.

53
00:02:45,470 --> 00:02:48,710
Work out 0.08 times 450.

54
00:02:48,760 --> 00:02:52,380
0.08 is 8 divided by 100.

55
00:02:52,430 --> 00:02:54,800
8 times 450 is 3,600.

56
00:02:54,850 --> 00:02:56,420
Divide by 100.

57
00:02:56,470 --> 00:02:58,930
The answer is 36.

58
00:02:58,980 --> 00:03:02,000
Work out 7.2 divided by 30.

59
00:03:02,050 --> 00:03:06,400
Dividing by 30 is dividing by 3, then by 10.

60
00:03:06,450 --> 00:03:09,000
7.2 divided by 3 is 2.4.

61
00:03:09,050 --> 00:03:12,900
Then 2.4 divided by 10 is 0.24.

62
00:03:12,950 --> 00:03:13,700
Your turn.

63
00:03:13,750 --> 00:03:15,880
Work out 8.4 divided by 20.

64
00:03:15,930 --> 00:03:19,060
Pause and work it out.

65
00:03:19,110 --> 00:03:21,490
Divide by 2, then by 10.

66
00:03:21,540 --> 00:03:23,930
8.4 divided by 2 is 4.2.

67
00:03:23,980 --> 00:03:27,630
Then 4.2 divided by 10 is 0.42.

68
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:30,120
A ticket costs 11 dollars 95.

69
00:03:30,170 --> 00:03:32,990
How much do 6 tickets cost?

70
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:35,270
Round up to 12 dollars.

71
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:37,510
6 times 12 is 72.

72
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:40,190
Each ticket was 5 cents too much.

73
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:43,000
6 times 5 cents is 30 cents.

74
00:03:43,050 --> 00:03:44,390
Take that off.

75
00:03:44,440 --> 00:03:46,660
72 minus 0.30 is 71.70.

76
00:03:46,710 --> 00:03:50,270
The tickets cost 71 dollars 70.

77
00:03:50,320 --> 00:03:54,180
Sam works out 9 times 3.4, using 10 times 3.4.

78
00:03:54,230 --> 00:03:57,100
Which line goes wrong first?

79
00:03:57,150 --> 00:03:58,490
Line 2 is wrong.

80
00:03:58,540 --> 00:04:02,210
9 lots is one lot of 3.4 less than 10 lots.

81
00:04:02,260 --> 00:04:04,750
So subtract 3.4, not 1.

82
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:08,000
34 minus 3.4 is 30.6.

83
00:04:08,050 --> 00:04:10,640
Shops love prices that end in 99.

84
00:04:10,690 --> 00:04:12,960
Compensation makes them easy.

85
00:04:13,010 --> 00:04:17,180
Suppose you buy 5 drinks at 3 dollars 99 each.

86
00:04:17,230 --> 00:04:20,090
Pretend each one costs 4 dollars.

87
00:04:20,140 --> 00:04:22,060
5 times 4 is 20.

88
00:04:22,110 --> 00:04:26,190
Each price was 1 cent too much, so take off 5 cents.

89
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:28,890
The total is 19 dollars 95.

90
00:04:28,940 --> 00:04:30,320
One last question.

91
00:04:30,370 --> 00:04:31,990
What is 99 times 0.3?

92
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:35,540
Pause the video and answer.

93
00:04:35,590 --> 00:04:37,690
100 times 0.3 is 30.

94
00:04:37,740 --> 00:04:41,140
That is one lot of 0.3 too many.

95
00:04:41,190 --> 00:04:43,960
30 minus 0.3 is 29.7.

96
00:04:44,010 --> 00:04:48,950
To remember: compensation means round, calculate, then adjust.

97
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:51,090
Split numbers or divisors.

98
00:04:51,140 --> 00:04:55,260
Dividing by 40 is dividing by 4, then by 10.

99
00:04:55,310 --> 00:04:59,650
Re-order to use easy pairs, like 0.25 times 4.

100
00:04:59,700 --> 00:05:02,210
And a decimal is a division.

101
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:05,040
0.06 is 6 divided by 100.

102
00:05:05,090 --> 00:05:10,190
Great work! Now practise lesson 4.5 on Camday.
